{"parentUuid":"442cb1c7-2c2b-4912-bca0-9c270e791107","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8c0f41b5-446a-49e2-8833-723d238c3f62","agentId":"abc21309eec17d1b7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018fHhsMQ8WepNxC5Vq1ipfz","type":"tool_result","content":"   \"mode\": \"harness\",\n   \"limits\": \"message schema\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"web-sources\",\n   \"validating_owner\": \"research-evidence\",\n   \"parser_owners\": [],\n   \"trust\": \"agent-input\",\n   \"mode\": \"redteam\",\n   \"limits\": \"provenance tiers\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"external-reports\",\n   \"validating_owner\": \"engine-product-management\",\n   \"parser_owners\": [\n    \"program-orchestration\"\n   ],\n   \"trust\": \"agent-input\",\n   \"mode\": \"redteam\",\n   \"limits\": \"quarantined as data\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"vuln-reports\",\n   \"validating_owner\": \"security-engineering\",\n   \"parser_owners\": [],\n   \"trust\": \"agent-input\",\n   \"mode\": \"redteam\",\n   \"limits\": \"quarantined as data\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"third-party-source\",\n   \"validating_owner\": \"build-system-toolchains\",\n   \"parser_owners\": [],\n   \"trust\": \"agent-input\",\n   \"mode\": \"redteam\",\n   \"limits\": \"pinned/verified\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"project-content-to-llm\",\n   \"validating_owner\": \"ai-assisted-authoring\",\n   \"parser_owners\": [],\n   \"trust\": \"agent-input\",\n   \"mode\": \"redteam\",\n   \"limits\": \"workspace trust\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n      [\n       \"BLD.REL.engine-distribution\",\n       \"Engine SDK/editor binary distribution & installers\",\n       \"packaging-release-patching\",\n       \"E\"\n      ],\n      [\n       \"BLD.REL.staged-rollout\",\n       \"Simultaneous global rollout to all players with post-release kill switches\",\n       \"packaging-release-patching\",\n       \"E\",\n       [\n        \"online-services-liveops\"\n       ]\n      ],\n      [\n     \"id\": \"QA.RENDER\",\n     \"name\": \"Rendering validation\",\n     \"caps\": [\n      [\n       \"QA.RENDER.golden\",\n       \"Golden-image tests with perceptual metrics (FLIP class)\",\n       \"render-validation\",\n       \"E\"\n      ],\n      [\n       \"QA.RENDER.matrix\",\n       \"GPU / driver matrix testing\",\n       \"render-validation\",\n       \"E\",\n       [\n        \"rhi-core\"\n       ]\n      ],\n      [\n       \"QA.RENDER.reference\",\n10636:       \"QA.SIM.netsim\",\n10637-       \"Deterministic single-process network-simulation runner, metrics & tolerance store\",\n10638-       \"simulation-validation\",\n10639-       \"E\",\n10640-       [\n10641-        \"prediction-rollback\",\n10642-        \"replication\"\n1:17:   \"test_double\": {\n7:23-   \"id\": \"C-ERR\",\n9:85:   \"test_double\": {\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:18:| A3 | Large-scale streaming for *authoring* (not just runtime) | Runtime streaming is well described (world partition docs, open-world GDC talks). Editor-side partial loading, and conflict-free editing at scale, is rarely published.\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:26:| A11 | Memory-safety posture for a C++ engine | Guidance exists (hardening modes, safe subsets, Rust interop), but there is little production evidence for engines specifically. | security-engineering, core-runtime-architect | ADR: w\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:30:| A13 | Validation of autonomous-agent-produced engine code | New discipline; little evidence on failure modes of agent-written systems code at this scale. | test-architect, program-orchestration | Mutation testing to detect vacuous \ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:60:| B23 | Physics middleware mode | In-house vs integrated middleware with an engine-side integration layer | physics-architect | Rewind/snapshot support, determinism level, source access (see PHY.ARCH.middleware-layer). |\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:22:| Orchestrator | 4 | `engine-architect` (boundaries, profiles, arbitration across workstreams), `architecture-governance` (ADRs, fitness functions, radar, anti-legacy catalogue, critic calibration, adjudication and the independe\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:42:- **No upward module links.** A runtime skill's code may only consume contracts at or below the layer of the module doing the consuming. A skill that ships several modules attributes each dependency to one of them. For example, \ndocs/00-design-principles.md:47:- **Data flow between subsystems.** Runtime data travels through **channels** (`C-FLOW`: versioned snapshots, buffered hand-off, mailboxes, multi-rate resampling) under an engine-wide **access model** (`C-FRAME`). Ordering is de\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:95:| The submission strategy is chosen per hardware tier by ADR. The GPU-driven path is the default on desktop and console. The CPU-culled batched path is first-class on TBDR/lite3d. 2D draws through batched draw lists by design. |\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:100:| No hidden globals: services and self-registration run through an init graph, and config is read through immutable snapshots. | Implicitly initialized singletons; global cvars read from any thread. | These are required for par\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:122:| Determinism, snapshot/resimulate and replay are one cross-cutting skill with three contracts: `C-DET` (L1 rules), `C-SNAPSHOT` (L2) and `C-REPLAY` (L3). | The properties hold only if every participant follows the same protoco\nC-PRESENT None\nC-SCENETEX None\nC-SHARD None\nC-SRVDATA None\n331:        \"test-architect\",\n360:        \"test-architect\"\n2877:        \"test-architect\"\n5679:        \"test-architect\"\n6237:        \"test-architect\"\n818:     \"render-validation\"\n838:   \"id\": \"render-validation\",\n3865:     \"render-validation\"","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"27829bf6-8146-4c32-b72f-8909265b6260","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:19:54.225Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"442cb1c7-2c2b-4912-bca0-9c270e791107","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8